{
  "name": "earwig",
  "_about": "The common earwig (Forficula auricularia), 1.5 cm long: long, flat and glossy chestnut; a flat heart-shaped head with beaded antennae; a square pronotum with pale side margins; short pale wing cases with the folded wings' tips peeping out behind; a long abdomen of overlapping segments ending in the forceps -- bowed calipers in the male, nearly straight in the female; pale yellowish legs. Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/insects/bugs.py on insectlib.py (jointed legs on a walking gait, the antennae on bones of their own that wave).",
